    description: "Observed in session_retrospective_04172026_1012.md Finding 1: the agent had 2 unread human messages (WI-ronot, WI-zikor) outstanding at its self-declared 'wrap', and its REPLY-FIRST CYCLE guidance (authored and merged in that same session, PR #3110) did not cause it to reply. REPLY-FIRST currently changes the stop-hook reason text and surfaces reply debt in guidance, but does not actually block stopping.\n\nProposed change: in scripts/tracker count-todos (or the stop hook that consumes it), treat unread human message count as an additional blocking condition in DEEP and BROAD modes. Zero unread messages becomes a precondition for stop, on equal footing with the TODO count. OFF mode is exempt.\n\nTouches .agent/hooks/** and scripts/tracker -> needs_human_review per governance rule."  # c196
